  "goodToKnow": "Good to know",
  "whyAiTitle": "Markdown and AI",
  "whyAiLede": "Markdown has quietly become the language models and people share. It is worth knowing why.",
  "whyAi1Title": "It is what the models already write",
  "whyAi1Body": "Ask ChatGPT, Claude or Gemini for anything structured and the answer comes back as Markdown — headings, bullets, tables, fenced code. Saving that reply as a .md file keeps it exactly as written, which is why so many people end up with a folder of them.",
  "whyAi2Title": "It is what they read best",
  "whyAi2Body": "A model sees your document as text. Hand it a PDF and the headings, columns and tables usually arrive as one flat run of words. Convert first and the structure arrives intact, so the model can tell a heading from a sentence and a table row from a paragraph.",
  "whyAi3Title": "It spends your context window on content",
  "whyAi3Body": "Word and HTML carry far more markup than text — tags, styles and identifiers the model must read and pay for. Markdown adds a handful of characters per heading. More of the window goes to what the document actually says.",
  "whyAi4Title": "It chunks along meaning",
  "whyAi4Body": "Retrieval pipelines split documents before searching them. With Markdown headings the splits fall at section boundaries instead of arbitrary page breaks, so a retrieved passage is a whole idea rather than half of two.",
  "whyAi5Title": "You can see everything you are about to send",
  "whyAi5Body": "An office file carries things you cannot see: tracked changes, resolved comments, author names, revision history, hidden sheets. Paste one into a chat and all of it goes along. A Markdown file is exactly what is on the screen — which matters most when the document was confidential to begin with.",
  "privacyTitle": "Privacy — your files are never collected",
  "privacyShort": "Nothing is uploaded, collected, or used to train any AI. Every conversion runs on this device.",
  "privacyLede": "Nothing you open here is uploaded, stored, logged or shared. Not with a server, not with an AI company, not with the developer.",
  "privacy1Title": "Your documents are never uploaded.",
  "privacy1Body": "They are read on this device, converted by code running on it, and gone when you leave the screen. There is no server to send them to.",
  "privacy2Title": "They are never used to train or prompt any AI.",
  "privacy2Body": "No model sees them. Nothing is sent to OpenAI, Anthropic, Google or anyone else. The conversion is ordinary parsing code, not a language model.",
  "privacy3Title": "The developer cannot see what you convert.",
  "privacy3Body": "Not by policy — by construction. There is no account, no database and no log, so there is nothing to look at even in principle.",
  "privacy4Title": "No analytics, no cookies, no tracking.",
  "privacy4Body": "The app contains no analytics or advertising code and opens no network connection of its own. The typeface is bundled with it rather than fetched from a font service.",
  "privacy5Title": "Only your settings are stored.",
  "privacy5Body": "Your conversion preferences, theme and language are kept on the device. Document content never is.",
  "privacyException": "The one exception, stated plainly: if a document you convert links to an image hosted on the web, the preview will load that image from wherever it lives, exactly as any viewer would. Set Images to “Leave out entirely” in Conversion settings if you would rather it never did.",
  "privacyVerify": "You can check all of this: turn off the network and convert a file. It still works, because there was never anything on the other end.",
